=== Source 2: Fictional diary extract (written for this exam)

#block(inset: 10pt, stroke: 0.5pt, width: 100%)[
_The following diary entry was written for this examination to represent the experience of a British infantry private. It is not a real document._

_"14 July 1916. We were told the bombardment would cut the wire and the Germans would be too dazed to fight. It went on for seven days. The ground shook every hour and the rain never stopped. When we went over the top at half past seven, the wire was still there in places and the machine guns were waiting. I saw the lad from Leeds next to me fall before we had gone twenty yards. I do not know how many of us came back. The officers say it was a success. I cannot see how."_
]

